= start | Quill Help | 1
# Quill Help
Quill is a rich-text word processor for DOS, Windows 3.1 and Windows 95, 98 and Me. Choose a topic.
- [Typing and editing](editing)
- [Formatting text](formatting)
- [Saving and opening documents](files)
- [Keyboard shortcuts](keys)
A [.QLD file](!qld) is Quill's own format.

= editing | Typing and editing | 10
# Typing and editing
Type where the caret is. Use the arrow keys, Home, End, Page Up and Page Down to move, and Backspace and Delete to remove text. **Ctrl+Z** undoes the last change and **Ctrl+Y** repeats it.
Choose Find from the Find menu to search; Replace changes every match you choose. [Back to the contents](start).

= formatting | Formatting text | 20
# Formatting text
**Ctrl+B** makes the selection bold, **Ctrl+I** italic and **Ctrl+U** underlined. The Format menu sets the font, the size, the colour, the alignment and the tab stops.
- Bullets and numbering come from the Format menu.
- A paragraph style sets a whole paragraph at once.
[Back to the contents](start).

= files | Saving and opening documents | 30
# Saving and opening documents
Quill saves its own [.QLD files](!qld) and reads and writes Rich Text Format (.RTF) and plain text. Choose Save As to pick the format. [Back to the contents](start).

= keys | Keyboard shortcuts | 40
# Keyboard shortcuts
- Ctrl+N new, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+S save
- Ctrl+X cut, Ctrl+C copy, Ctrl+V paste
- Ctrl+0 or Ctrl+numpad 0 Page Width (Alt+0 on DOS)
- Ctrl+numpad + zoom in, Ctrl+minus or Ctrl+numpad minus zoom out (Alt+numpad +, Alt+= and Alt+minus on DOS)
- Ctrl+wheel zooms on Windows 95 and later
- Ctrl+Page Up and Ctrl+Page Down scroll the page three lines without moving the caret (DOS)
- F7 checks the spelling
- F1 opens this help
[Back to the contents](start).

= qld | QLD file
A QLD file is Quill's native document format. It keeps text, styles and pictures, and it can be recovered after a crash.
